better|REVIEW: [LEXICAL_IDENTITY] Higher-quality adjective and worked-better adverb accurately represent good/well comparatives. The nominal for the better boundary is source-supported but construction-bound; owner should decide how it relates to good/well and phrase teaching before canonical identity allocation. Vietnamese retains the leadership improvement without fabricating an independent countable noun.
humid|PASS: Water vapour in air and post-shower example support có độ ẩm cao. Vietnamese không khí, rather than wet ground, preserves the target. Humidity note correctly distinguishes air moisture from a surface being wet.
lump|PASS: Compact irregular clay piece matches cục and the bucket context. Vietnamese preserves remaining material. The broad source gloss also mentions swelling, but this definition does not silently claim medical lump coverage or diagnose anything.
rust|REVIEW: [GRAMMAR] Iron/steel corrosion and hinge example are accurate, with uncountable material expressed as rỉ sét. grammarNotesEn's final separate POS proposal comment belongs to tooling rather than learner content; replace it with a concise verb-usage contrast by overlay.
stricken|PASS: Harmful-event adjective and storm-stricken village match the source English boundary better than its literal hit bruised gloss. Vietnamese retains aid items and severe storm effects. With/by and ordinary struck-versus-adjectival stricken distinguish usage without denying literary variants.
